# --- Local reference docs not for version control ---
docs/reference/domain reference Overview_2021_FEP.pdf

# --- Engine's own lockfile: intentionally NOT committed (verified 2026-07-07, not inherited from
# generic policy). This org's only path to npm is the internal Nexus mirror; confirmed empirically
# that Nexus rewrites every dependency's lockfile `resolved` tarball URL to embed its own hostname
# (there is no direct route to the public registry to avoid it). Committing the lockfile as-is would
# put an internal host literal in every entry, failing the same host-literal bar enforced elsewhere
# in this repo. Reproducibility is instead achieved by exact-pinning root devDependencies (see
# package.json — no `^` ranges) plus `npm install` (not `npm ci`) in the engine's own Jenkinsfile.
# Consumer projects are unaffected: they commit their own lockfile and use `npm ci` normally, since
# their per-system CI environment is expected to resolve that host once, in their own repo.
# workspace files embed local paths, so those stay ignored too.
package-lock.json
*.code-workspace
